The development of single shot approaches to object detection, such as SSD, YOLO, and RetinaNet<|CIT-MASK|> allow for objects to be localized up to their bounding boxes within a given image. The FCN, U-Net, and DeepLab architectures<|CIT-MASK|>, among others, developed for semantic segmentation, allow for pixel-wise categorical classification.

